  Trace Files — results/
  
  Every single query saves a JSON file: results/trace_<8hex>.json
  
  Open any one and you'll see:
  
  - query — what was asked
  - agent_evidence — what each agent retrieved, their status, claims, sources
  - evidence_decision — state, pairwise NLI scores, top conflict
  - conflict — type, explanation, the two conflicting claims
  - debate_rounds — each round's proposer/critic/reviser content
  - judge_result — winner, reason, scores
  - final_answer — the text shown to user
  - metrics — latency, LLM calls by role, evidence state, etc.

